WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:07.000
It possesses enormous power,
and brings endless pleasure

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.960
and destruction  to those who are destined.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.720
The Witchblade.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.800
At this moment, one woman has awakened.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.460
Just before the shot, my chest feels like it's gonna tear open

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.050
I shout out countless times, break out

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:42.240
It's not over, rush through the endless night

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.530
Hot blood flows through my body

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:51.240
The moment it ultimately rots away

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:57.840
it's all over, fragments of an empty dream come to mind

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:03.340
I can never go back, I can't remember a thing

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.880
I've been reduced to struggling, and my voice won't carry

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.390
Uncontrollable impulses

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:19.310
Give me your XTC, let me feel it one more time

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:26.530
This body heats up, and I shout out your name in the darkness

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:33.530
Give me your XTC, I don't need false love

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.710
I will accept it, sin and punishment

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:43.280
Slash through the destiny I've been set up with, Blade

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:52.610
"Interaction"

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:53.730
Morning!

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.150
Good morning!

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:58.700
That smells great!

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.950
Yours is on the table.

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.700
I'm gonna deliver this,
so go ahead and eat first!

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.910
'Kay, see you in a bit!

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.290
That wakes me up!

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.050
Hey, you around?

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.130
What the ?! Can't you at least knock?!

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:21.180
You're all filthy,
first thing in the morning...

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.430
Quiet. I was up all night workin'.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.140
Where's your daughter?
With Chou-san.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:30.940
In that case, I can talk openly.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:35.690
I pulled up documents on Douji
Industries from the newspaper office.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.730
I got a connection there, ya see...

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:40.530
Anyways, it's a big-time corporation.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:44.120
So big, in fact, that other groups
try to bring it down once in a while.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.160
Why's that?

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:49.250
Ain't it obvious? Douji's a known
weapons manufacturer and exporter.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:56.920
You're involved with a Douji director,
yet you don't even know that?!

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.880
I just wasn't interested, until now.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:05.640
So, from what you say, I-Weapons
are probably weapons they export.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.100
It's probably a huge issue for peace freaks,

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.100
but it won't make much of a story by itself.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:15.110
But it's a whole different story
if those weapons are actually people,

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.570
like that guy yesterday.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:21.700
Yeah. I had always assumed they
were machines in human form, but...

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:25.410
I'll ask Takayama about it directly!

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.410
Talk about cutting to the chase...

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:30.830
I want to know the truth too, you know!

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.790
Alright. Then I'll attack from another angle.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:38.630
First are the NSWF Neo-Genes you talked about.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:40.300
This is gonna get interesting!

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:44.840
Let's have a taste!

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:47.720
Sweet!

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:51.100
I used maple syrup today
instead of powdered sugar!

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:56.270
Such delicate sweetness!
And this soft-boiled-ness is great!

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.780
Everything you make
is so yummy, Rihoko-Chan!

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.610
Oh, uhh...

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:06.660
Of course, you make
great coffee yourself, Missy!

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.950
Have you gotten better at brewing it?!

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:12.160
I got a new coffeemaker.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:17.290
No, no, you have real heart
when you press the button, you do!

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.170
Oh, it's Tozawa-Chan.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:27.550
Hey! Don't forget our
group date with the nice gals!

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:28.850
I won't!

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:31.180
Say, are group dates that fun?

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:32.180
You bet!

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:37.980
They're miracle events of destiny
where men and women get to meet!

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:39.440
Morning!

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:44.440
Morning, Masamune-Chan!
Want some of Missy's delicious coffee?

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.780
Thanks, but I gotta get going.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:51.370
Riko, I should be home by
tonight, but I'll call you later!

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:54.120
Wait, Mom. Are you going out like that?

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.250
Something not right?

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:00.040
You still have bed-head! You need
to pay more attention to your looks!

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:02.170
Nah, that's okay!

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.800
See you later!
See ya!

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:11.760
And the lab report meeting is
scheduled to end at 1 5:00. Tonight is

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:13.720
Cancel all plans for tonight.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:14.770
Eh?

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:21.860
Oh, this is an invitation to
the Bio-Section's celebratory party.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:25.860
Yes, Wadou-san was sending e-mails
all over the place, bragging about

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:29.660
how his research team won the
International Science Foundation Prize.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:33.080
Oh? But this isn't addressed to you...

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:37.210
No, the head of Motor
Vehicles passed it on to me.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:40.630
Here's the main attendance list.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:44.800
What's this? They're all officials
deeply involved with our section,

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.720
and big shots of affiliate companies...

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:50.260
Sounds like something Wadou would do.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:55.890
I see. They're all people he
intends to add to his clique. Clever.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:02.770
Well, I doubt he'll do much of anything,
but I thought I'd drop by, too.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:06.280
To keep him in check? Understood.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.650
I'll change your plans for tonight.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:13.870
And shall I prepare you a
high-class partner? An actress, perhaps?

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:14.990
An actress?

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:18.710
It says here to bring a partner.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:21.250
If you don't act the part out,

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:26.590
your lack of an invitation will make
it seem like you're a party-crasher.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:31.430
Wadou-san always brings
actresses and models to parties,

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:33.970
so you need to bring a good companion, too.

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:37.310
Morning.

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:40.140
Good morning! What's wrong?

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.230
I have something I want to ask.

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:48.740
What is this, all of a sudden?

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:50.990
About the X-Cons...

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:53.410
What about them?

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.120
They're...

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:01.210
...human, aren't they?

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:08.760
What makes you think that?

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:12.590
I met someone who knew
the guy I destroyed yesterday.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:13.550
I see.

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:17.510
So you don't deny it?
Does that mean I-Weapons are too?!

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.770
Yes, they are.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:21.270
Sir!

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:25.020
There's no point in
trying to hide it. Tell her.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.400
As you wish...

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:33.860
It's been a long time, Father.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.700
Reina, whatever is the matter?

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:39.450
Ever since Shiori's unfortunate accident,

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:44.120
you've lost your passion
for acquiring the Witchblade...

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:47.710
I have other interesting research, you see.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.130
Even more so than the Witchblade?

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:51.880
In my eyes, at least...

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:57.350
What a shame. Even after
the Witchblade chose you, too...

00:07:57.430 --> 00:08:02.100
And that is why you think of me as cute.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:07.690
But of course. There is no parent
who wouldn't adore a chosen child.

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:12.150
Adore? What sort of emotion might that be?

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:15.530
What's wrong? Why do you suddenly say that?

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:21.870
No, I was simply curious.
Please use other sisters for the Witchblade.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:26.750
I'll be leaving your side
for a while. Goodbye, Father.

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:36.720
I guess I pampered her a little too much...

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.390
It would appear that way.

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:43.140
Well, then. What to do...

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:47.810
In short, it'd be more precise to
call I-Weapons and low-class X-Cons

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:52.650
"former people" rather than "people."

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:53.940
What do you mean?

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:55.860
They're dead people.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:59.780
They have all sorts of backgrounds.

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:03.120
We make agreements with
some people while they're alive,

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:06.410
or with their families after death.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:10.630
What?! You know it's not
right to use people like that!

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:13.670
Well, they are given considerable compensation.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:15.800
But you sell them as weapons!

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:17.840
Well, it is business.

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:21.850
That's sick! And you're only
helping wars break out by selling

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:25.350
Wars are not caused by weapons.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:30.400
People have fought since prehistory.
War will never disappear.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:33.690
Instead, we need to limit
casualties to the bare minimum.

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:36.110
And that's what I-Weapons are for?

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:41.700
Overwhelming power can end
wars quickly, or even deter them.

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:45.660
I-Weapons also only require
the bare minimum of soldiers.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:49.420
But... But they're still people!

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:55.380
Aren't you fighting to keep those
living people from being harmed?

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:02.470
You know how to talk when it
comes to money, but that's about it.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:06.680
Anyway, I have something to ask you.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:08.810
According to the recovery team's report,

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:12.400
you were with an outsider
when you took care of the X-Con.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:17.650
Oh, he lives in the same building
as me! He just happened to, uhh

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.610
Has he found out?

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:22.870
Well, uhh...

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.780
So he has.

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:29.790
It would really help if you
told us these things sooner.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:31.710
Don't tell me you're gonna shut him up?!

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:36.250
Nothing of the sort!
We simply wish to grasp the situation.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:42.390
A photographer or two
aren't any cause for concern.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.180
However... you'll have to pay the penalty.

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:47.310
Eh?!

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:51.650
Segawa, take her to the best store you know.

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.810
Turn this boor into someone presentable.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:59.110
Who're you calling a boor?!
You're a gloomy gorilla yourself!

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.820
First, stop talking like that.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:04.780
Next, stop going out
looking like you just woke up.

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:07.620
Mind your own business! I'm going home!

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:11.710
I told you, this is your penalty.
Or would you rather pay monetarily?

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.630
Fine.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.790
Segawa, put it on my card. Next.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:58.210
Come on! Explain already!
What in the world is this "penalty"?!

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:05.590
Don't use long strides. Don't talk loudly.
Call me "Sir." Got that?

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:08.140
What's going on? Ugh!

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:26.950
I'm sorry for always doing this...

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:32.250
It's no problem at all!
Just don't drink too much, now! Bye!

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:34.330
Masamune-Chan's going to be late?

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:39.170
Yeah. So let's have dinner together!
I'll make us something!

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:45.380
Really?! Lucky! I get to have
some more of your homemade food!

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:49.760
Say, why don't we just have a party?
The kitchen is big...

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:51.390
I'd love that!

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:54.230
That okay with you, Missy?

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:58.730
Most certainly is.
I think I'll make something, too...

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:02.650
That pose... She's all fired up!

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:03.900
Eh?

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:10.700
Director Wadou!
Congratulations on winning the ISF Prize!

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:11.990
Thank you.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.790
Your Bio-Section is the
face of the company now!

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.750
If only we could all take after you!

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:22.710
No, the Bio-Section I have in
mind is nothing like this at all.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:23.760
Ah!

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:27.720
I haven't worked with your
Machines Department much thus far,

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:30.930
but I'd very much like to
work with you in the future.

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:33.010
Of course! Just say the word!

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:34.720
Sir.

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:38.650
There's Director Takayama.
What?!

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:42.860
How dare he just waltz in here...

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:46.280
Umm, excuse me, but may I see your invitation?

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.950
I'm Takayama, director of the Special Section.

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:50.620
You've never heard of him?!

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:54.240
Director Takayama! It's good to see you again!

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:55.830
Forgive my rudeness.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:01.290
Congratulations on the award, Wadou-san.

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:03.710
Oh, how nice of you to come.

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:09.380
I didn't get an invitation, but I figured
it was just some sort of mistake.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:14.850
Absurd! My section would
never make any kind of mistake

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:21.860
Beautiful...

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:25.400
Takayama-kun, who is this beautiful woman?

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:30.610
Oh, she's a distant relative
of mine, Amaha Masane.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.660
A distant relative? Yeah, sure.

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:38.580
Dressing me up like this as a "penalty."
I bet he actually likes me!

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:41.170
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:46.710
No, uhh, the invitation thing was
probably a clerical error on my part.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.880
I apologize, Takayama-kun.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:51.130
That's all right.

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:53.640
What's that?! Look at all the food!

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:55.180
Woo-hoo!

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:02.270
Can I eat this?!
As much as you'd like.

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:04.770
Then I'll take that!
Certainly.

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:10.860
Hey, now! Please don't embarrass
the director in front of Wadou-san!

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:14.070
What's the big deal?
You're the ones who dragged me here!

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:18.160
Why did Takayama bring me here, anyway?!

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:21.040
He needs a partner to put on his act.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:22.420
Oh, that's why?

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:25.790
In any case, please behave yourself.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:26.840
Here you are.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:31.300
Oh, so anyone would've done. How rude of him!

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:34.340
Sir! The former prime minister is here!

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:36.300
What's a big name like him doing here?

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:40.680
You don't know? He was the
head judge for the ISF Prize.

00:15:40.770 --> 00:15:43.980
Eh?! Does that mean this award was

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:48.270
Guess there's no doubt Wadou's
been sending political funds his way.

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:52.150
Once again, we present this crystal plaque,

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:56.160
a great honor and symbol of the ISF Prize!

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:01.330
Wow!

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:03.580
I gotta bring some home for Riko!

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:06.290
Hey, can I get these in a box?!

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:08.750
Certainly.

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:10.800
Lucky! Okay, let's find some more!

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:17.140
The crystal plaque!
Oww...

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:18.930
What?!

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:23.430
I'm so sorry! Was that important

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:25.810
Of course it was!

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:27.860
I-I'm really sorry!

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:31.820
Apologizing won't fix this!
What do you have to say for yourself?!

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:34.320
I'll pay for it.
What?

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:37.240
I'll pay for it. How much was it?

00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:39.370
How much? You can't be serious...

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:41.080
Just tell me how much!

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:43.830
Too much for some oaf like you!

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:46.210
No, tell us.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:50.840
I'll help her out. I did bring her, after all.

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:55.590
But Takayama-kun, this isn't
something that is easily compensated

00:16:55.680 --> 00:17:01.930
Don't worry. If that gentleman
can tell us how much you paid for it,

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:03.980
I'm sure I can gather that amount right away.

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:05.730
What did you say?!

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:16.780
I'm only joking.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.450
What a harsh joke!

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:27.710
Let's go!

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:35.880
I'm afraid you can't reimburse
me, Miss. This isn't about money.

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:37.880
It's a matter of honor.

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:42.140
You really are a man of
great caliber, Wadou-san...

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:48.100
Remember how we handled things in college?

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:50.270
We'll settle this that way!

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:57.320
What? Wadou-san and
Takayama-san?! Are you serious?!

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:19.970
Hold on! Don't do this because of me!
It's not good to drink like that!

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:23.550
Are you worried about me?
Y-Yeah, right!

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:27.140
Never fear. We used to do this all the time.

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:28.100
Seriously?!

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:32.730
Though it was always you
who got smashed first...

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:38.240
Is he gonna be alright?!

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:41.860
No, Wadou-san is famous for his heavy drinking.

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:45.700
The director is at a disadvantage.
You can't be serious!

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:49.660
Oh, my! This is a breathtaking battle!

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:59.760
W-What incredible intensity!
But it smells really good!

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:03.850
Incredible...

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:09.140
How can this be?!

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:14.190
Why won't he fall?!

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:31.250
He won!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.330
Sir! Say something!

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:40.670
Segawa, tend to Director Wadou.
Yes, sir...

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:42.720
Let's go.
Eh?!

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:45.180
I'm done here.
There's no need to linger around.

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:47.180
T-There isn't?

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:53.060
Hold on! Wait for me!

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:59.570
So you are drunk.
Though that's to be expected...

00:19:59.650 --> 00:20:02.780
Seeing you get wasted...
I guess you Can be cute sometimes!

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:05.990
Cute? Me?

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:07.490
Cute?

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:11.580
Maybe compared to a boor like you...

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:17.960
What?! You're the one who
dragged that boor along! How rude!

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:22.720
I'm not being rude. I like boors...

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:26.090
Eh? Y-You do?

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:30.180
Don't go to sleep!

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:33.940
Oh, geez...

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:40.520
So cold!

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:47.820
Rihoko's omelet and Missy's pizza...
Hard to say which is better!

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:50.580
This one's delicious,
and this one's scrumptious!

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.580
Yes, exactly!
It's the IT revolution of cooking!

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:55.500
You're pretty good.
You too, Mariko-san!

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:10.720
How are the girls doing?
Perfectly.

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:13.810
The Cloneblade upgrade is coming along too,

00:21:13.890 --> 00:21:16.690
but I absolutely need the
original Witchblade for that...

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:20.730
I understand. We should have it soon.

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:25.650
Thank you. I will show you
one that surpasses the original.

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:27.700
I look forward to it.

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:38.830
This girl will surpass all...

00:21:57.190 --> 00:22:07.280
I murmur, "I love you," with all my emotion

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:16.620
All my feelings until yesterday now overflow and dissolve quickly

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:28.550
If only this one last prayer could make it through...

00:22:28.630 --> 00:22:37.390
Thank you for giving us the words to ascertain each other, God

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:49.400
Tomorrow, we'll reach out and hold hands harder than normal

00:22:49.490 --> 00:23:02.420
Tomorrow, we'll reach out, hug, kiss, and love each other

00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:15.180
You drink too much at parties, Mom!

00:23:15.260 --> 00:23:17.060
You know you shouldn't drink!

00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:18.390
You get drunk so easily!

00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:21.560
You're finally wearing a pretty dress,
and it goes to waste!

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:25.560
You didn't come home,
so Chou-san and the others were worried!

00:23:25.650 --> 00:23:29.110
But I'm glad I finally got to meet your boss!

00:23:29.190 --> 00:23:32.610
You talked bad about him,
but I really like him!

00:23:32.700 --> 00:23:34.870
He's much better than Tozawa-chan!

00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:36.990
He'd probably be even better
if he didn't have a hangover!

00:23:37.080 --> 00:23:39.870
You should marry him, Mom!
